  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msub></math> (methylene) groups in the product formed from the following reaction sequence is _____ .</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/a7edbc51-7d35-4cba-af2f-72cf7eff5780-image.png\" style=\"width: 442px; height: 120px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "0",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The first reaction is called reductive ozonolysis in which alkene is converted into aldehyde of ketones. In 2nd reaction aldehyde group will be oxidised to carboxylic acid.&nbsp;</p><p>The third reaction is called Kolbe&#39;s electrolysis reaction in which decarboxylation reaction will occur forming higher alkane.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/317cbebe-129a-4d1d-8c6d-267d0bbfe8ed-image.png\" style=\"width: 472px; height: 350px;\" /></p><p>In last step of reaction aromatisation&nbsp;reaction will take place forming benzene as the major product. This benzene does not contain any&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;group.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
